# SwiftUI Conventions

Follow `SWIFTUI_BEST_PRACTICES.md`. Full details live there; these are the non-negotiables.

**Sheets:** use `sheet(item:)` for optional-data sheets. `sheet(isPresented:)` only for simple toggles with no payload. Same idea for `navigationDestination(item:)` and `fullScreenCover(item:)`.

```swift
// ❌ BAD — two states + onChange sync
@State private var editingEvent: SyncableEvent?
@State private var showEditSheet = false
.sheet(isPresented: $showEditSheet) {
    if let event = editingEvent { CreateItemSheet(editingEvent: event) }
}

// ✅ GOOD — item is the source of truth
@State private var editingEvent: SyncableEvent?
.sheet(item: $editingEvent) { event in
    CreateItemSheet(editingEvent: event)
}
```

**State:** single source of truth. If `showSheet` is always `true` when `selectedItem != nil`, keep only `selectedItem`. Do not use `onChange` to keep two variables in sync.

**Queries:** filter at the `@Query` level, not in the view body.

```swift
// ✅ GOOD
@Query(filter: #Predicate<SyncableEvent> { !$0.isDeleted }, sort: \.startDate)
private var events: [SyncableEvent]

// ❌ BAD — refetch-all then filter on every render
@Query private var allEvents: [SyncableEvent]
var events: [SyncableEvent] { allEvents.filter { !$0.isDeleted } }
```
